\guide[name="document-paragraphs", part="word/document.xml", format="paragraphs", boundary=":::DEDOCS_GUIDE_1_63ba19b0f4dc:::"]
:::DEDOCS_GUIDE_1_63ba19b0f4dc:::
\p[index="0000", style="Heading1"] Introduction
\p[index="0001"] This is the first paragraph of the introduction. It contains some text about platform governance, political advertising, and auditability.
\p[index="0002"] The second paragraph discusses Meta's advertising ban and its consequences for electoral transparency.
\p[index="0003", style="Heading1"] Methods
\p[index="0004"] Table 1. Example metrics
\p[index="0005"] Metric
\p[index="0006"] Value
\p[index="0007"] Ads collected
\p[index="0008"] 268,635
\p[index="0009"] Confirmed advertisers
\p[index="0010"] 192
\p[index="0011"] This inserted paragraph shows how dedocs adds body text without raw XML edits.
\p[index="0012"] We developed an automated monitoring system that collected 268,635 advertisements from the Meta Ad Library.
\p[index="0013"] This inserted paragraph lands before Results and stays anchored by expectations.
\p[index="0014", style="Heading1"] Results
\p[index="0016"] Figure 1. Synthetic reference image
\p[index="0017"] We confirmed 192 accounts as political advertisers that placed a total of 1,329 ads during the campaign period.
\p[index="0018", style="Heading1"] Discussion
\p[index="0019"] The findings document a specific failure mode of platform self-regulation.
:::DEDOCS_GUIDE_1_63ba19b0f4dc:::
\end{guide}

